 "provenance": "Tibet 7 (world 2, level 6) normal exit 9,22, control-only from spawn on the exact S700 core. Start values: weaponTier 8 (ice hammer obtained in Tibet 6 at chest 32,22; Tibet 7+ may start with it), maxHealth 4 (no armor), lives 12 (campaign value used by the old routes), 0 diamonds. Route: walk up the column-3 grass (the two statues drop behind into the shaft) to checkpoint 1 (5,8); step into the statue beam at 7,9 so the frozen hero falls into the pocket (1 damage), break free, move to 8,10 and hook the statue at 6,9-10 to 7,9-10, then climb out through 8,9 during the 40-frame post-thaw invulnerability; go right along row 10 under the ceiling traps (no hit), wait at 28,10 for the ice creature, freeze it with the ice hammer and push the ice block onto plate 27,10 (gate 0 opens), checkpoint 2 (31,10); go up to 34,3, hook the weight so it lands at 33,4 (off the bridge), hammer the bridge switch 30,3 (all bridges toggle: 14,22 opens); return along rows 10/8 to 6,8, step into the statue's left beam at 6,9 (frozen fall to 6,10, 1 damage), break the bricks of column 6 with the hammer, enter the key area, walk into the chest 17,22 (gold key), cross the opened bridge 14,22, open the gold lock 10,21 and leave through gate 4 to exit 9,22. Health 4 -> 2, no deaths, no resets.",
